    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nnew\n\n### Description\n\nno-neck-pain.nvim toggles a scratch buffer on either side of the current buffer, making it easier to read code especially on larger monitors since it will usually get aligned to the left, and allows you to take notes in said scratch buffers.\n\n<img width=\"2420\" height=\"1398\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f63803c2-319c-4b90-83c7-f7c814e2da57\" />",
